HomotopyLieAlgebra -- Homotopy Lie Algebra of a surjective ring homomorphism
****************************************************************************

Description
===========

If R = S/I, K is the Koszul complex on the generators of I, and A is the
DGAlgebra that is the acyclic closure of K, then the homotopy Lie algebra Pi of
the map S -->> R is defined as in Briggs ****, with underlying vector space the
graded dual of the space spanned by a given set of generators of A.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[x,y]                      |
|                                          |
|o1 = S                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = S/ideal(x^2,y^2,x*y)             |
|                                          |
|o2 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o2 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : KR = koszulComplexDGA(ideal R)       |
|                                          |
|o3 = {Ring => S                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => S[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,3  |
|                        2   2             |
|      Differential => {x , y , x*y}       |
|                                          |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+

Since the acyclic closure is infinitely generated, we must specify the maximum
homological degree in which cycles will be killed

