ad -- matrix of the adjoint action
**********************************

  * Usage: 
        M = ad(A,U,e)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: (DGAlgebras)DGAlgebra,, 
      * U, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, linear form in the
        generators of A
      * e, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with entries in the ground
        field

Description
===========

The adjoint action of a scalar linear combination of the entries of
allgens(A,d-1) U, regarded as an element of Pi^d, acts by bracket
multiplication with source Pi^e and target Pi^{d+e}. The output is a matrix
whose columns correspond to a generalized row of the output of bracketMatrix.
bracketmatrix

