bracketMatrix -- Multiplication matrix of the homotopy Lie algebra
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = bracketMatrix(A,d,e)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: (DGAlgebras)DGAlgebra,,
        first part of the acyclic closure of a Koszul complex
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * e, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of linear forms in the
        generators of A

Description
===========

This function implements the multiplication table of the degree d and degree e
components of the homotopy Lie algebra Pi. The entries of the matrix are linear
forms of homological degree d+e+1, interpreted as generators of Pi^{d+e}. See
*note bracket: bracket, for more details.

